# 12. The abstraction you should memorize

Forget the individual API names for a moment.

Almost every LLM request can be understood as:

```text
┌───────────────────────────────────────┐
│              REQUEST                  │
│                                       │
│  Input                               │
│  ├── System instructions             │
│  ├── User message                   │
│  ├── Conversation history            │
│  ├── Documents                       │
│  └── Tool results                    │
│                                       │
│  Generation controls                  │
│  ├── Temperature                     │
│  ├── Top-P                            │
│  ├── Top-K                            │
│  ├── Max output tokens               │
│  └── Stop sequences                  │
└──────────────────┬────────────────────┘
                   │
                   ▼
                LLM
                   │
                   ▼
              Output tokens
                   │
                   ▼
             Final response
```

This abstraction works whether you're using OpenAI, Claude, Gemini, Llama, Mistral, DeepSeek or a model through Bedrock.

